---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="singletenant.ai is an independent buyer's resource for single-tenant LLM hosting, edited by Simon Newton."
>
  <section class="border-b border-[var(--color-rule)]">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-3">About</p>
      <h1 class="m-0 mb-6" style="font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);">
        Independent. Specific. Useful.
      </h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="drop-cap">
          singletenant.ai is an independent buyer's resource for single-tenant
          LLM hosting — written for engineering leaders, procurement teams, and
          compliance officers shipping AI inside boundaries that matter.
        </p>

        <p>
          The category is real but the buyer side of the market is poorly
          served. Vendor pages oversell. Analyst reports lag the technology.
          Reddit threads are rumour. We exist to fill the gap with regularly-
          updated vendor profiles, honest comparisons, and analysis grounded in
          real procurement and operational experience.
        </p>

        <h2>Edited by Simon Newton</h2>

        <p>
          I run the editorial here. My background: seven years leading global
          product delivery at Ocado Technology, where I shipped infrastructure
          rollouts across multiple territories under operational and compliance
          constraints; before that, the British Army and reconstruction
          programmes in Iraq.
        </p>

        <p>
          I now consult on AI delivery for compliance-heavy buyers — financial
          services, healthcare, defence, public sector — where the question is
          rarely "which model is best" and almost always "which deployment
          architecture clears legal, security, and procurement at the same
          time".
        </p>

        <h2>Editorial principles</h2>

        <p>
          <strong>Vendor neutrality.</strong> Some links on this site earn
          referral commission; we always disclose this clearly on the relevant
          pages. Commission never determines coverage. Our directory includes
          vendors with no partnership relationship.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Data first.</strong> Every vendor profile is grounded in
          structured data we maintain ourselves. We cite sources, mark review
          dates, and update profiles when material changes happen.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Specific, not generic.</strong> "Best LLM hosting for 2026"
          listicles aren't useful. We write for the buyer with a defined
          deployment context — a regulated industry, a compliance regime, a
          specific scale of workload. If a piece could apply to anyone, we
          haven't done our job.
        </p>

        <h2>Talk to us</h2>

        <p>
          Vendor news, factual corrections, partnership enquiries, or
          consulting requests — all welcome at <a href="mailto:simon@singletenant.ai">simon@singletenant.ai</a>.
          For consulting specifically, the <a href="/contact/">consulting
          page</a> has more detail.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
